  {
    "episode_id": 87422,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/7/87422.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "It's infrastructure summer in Washington. President Joe Biden came into office promising a major new investment in public works that make our nation go. Our highways, transit, ports, water systems, broadband, the electric grid, and so much more. And plans have been working their way through Congress, the House of Representatives passed an infrastructure package on July 1. Now, all eyes are on the United States Senate. There's the possibility of a bipartisan framework. Or if that doesn't pan out, Senate Democrats may go it alone. That's why we are very fortunate to have Senator Tammy Baldwin of Wisconsin on the podcast this episode. Senator Baldwin serves on the Senate Committee on Commerce, Science and Transportation, as well as the Appropriations Committee. She's been a powerful advocate for manufacturing in Wisconsin and across the nation. She's authored several important by America bills to ensure that our tax dollars are reinvested in workers right here. My interview with Senator Baldwin next on the Manufacturing Report. Senator Baldwin, welcome to the Manufacturing Report.",
