    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. And there is really no better person to talk to than you. I think for a couple of reasons. You've been a longstanding advocate for manufacturing. Wisconsin is a very manufacturing intensive state as you and I both know. You're on the Senate committee that deals with transportation issues as well as the appropriations committee. So you have a great perch from which to view all of this. And so, you know, we know Senator Biden, now President Biden came into office saying that he wanted to be an infrastructure president, wanted to pass a major new and that important to the economy of Wisconsin and to Wisconsin's workers.",
