  {
    "episode_id": 87422,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/7/87422.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "I will say I believe it is a strong bipartisan issue. I have been joined by Republicans from other intensive manufacturing states in by America policies and reforms for years now. And I am waging this fight to make sure we have strong by America policies in the bipartisan infrastructure framework and budget bill. engage in this fight with Republicans. If anything, it's more of a regional issue of gaining strong support from those states that skin industrial manufacturing base and recognizing that that's a key part of our economy. I was talking just a little bit before about what the pandemic taught us about the need for various things. The pandemic, because it was a global pandemic, taught us that if we don't make it here, we're going to have trouble getting it because the competition is going to be throughout the world. And whether that was personal protective equipment like N95 masks or things that we need to maintain our infrastructure to build automobiles and appliances, if that supply chain is outsourced, we are in a world of hurt. And the pandemic was really instructive in that regard. And I think we find ourselves in a moment where there's a heightened awareness of how important it is that we're able to fend for ourselves and make things ourselves.",
