  },
  {
    "episode_id": 87422,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/7/87422.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. Resilient supply change or something that I think you and I have understood for a long time, but that more folks are catching on to now just about how important that is because of some of the semiconductor chip shortages we've seen as you mentioned the PPE. And just as we look ahead, the need to make these massive investments in our economy and our infrastructure. in particular. I wanted to look ahead a second and if you're willing to share with our listeners your thoughts on this. So the House of Representatives has passed an infrastructure bill in July 1st. They're active conversations in the Senate about the bipartisan framework or other possibilities and the budget, as you mentioned, moving ahead. How optimistic are you that we can get infrastructure across the finish line here, because I do think that there have been expectations that have been significantly raised. And in the past, you know, infrastructure week was kind of a joke, right? You know, particularly in the last administration. But there's so much more focus and seriousness in leadership. Can we get this done this year, Senator Baldwin?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
